+# Feature Review
+
+> Strategic / business-model reviews of PuneNest features and thesis, written from a
+> **skeptical VC + PropTech strategist** perspective. These are **advisory analyses to review
+> and implement later** — not architecture decisions (those live in
+> [`../system/platform-architecture.md`](../system/platform-architecture.md)).
+>
+> **Author:** architecture partner (AI) · **Date:** 2026-07-26 · **Status:** for founder review
+
+## Contents
+
+| # | Doc | What it answers |
+|---|-----|-----------------|
+| 01 | [`01-business-model-kyc-thesis.md`](./01-business-model-kyc-thesis.md) | *"Why haven't established players solved spam/KYC? What am I not seeing? Will my product work?"* — a brutal critique of the mandatory-KYC-everywhere thesis for the **buy/rent** market. Verdict: **Pivot**. |
+| 02 | [`02-share-a-flat-market-and-feature-review.md`](./02-share-a-flat-market-and-feature-review.md) | *"Will share-a-flat drive the IT/young crowd? What's the market size and how do we take share?"* — market sizing + feature review of the flat-share segment. Verdict: **This is the wedge — lead with it.** |
+
+## How to use these
+
+1. Read `01` first — it frames *why* the plain "verify everyone" idea is risky on the core market.
+2. Read `02` — it shows the **one segment (flat-share) where the KYC obsession becomes an asset**, and how to go to market.
